        <p>To-day's matches are : Sankey v Wilderspool Brewery. St. Helens Cable Co. v Wbitecross. Rylands v Warrington Conservatives. Cairo-street v Walker's.</p>
        <p>The Warrington and District Sunday School League is filling a very useful place in local cricket circles and bids fiir to have a very useful and successful season. On Saturday there were several interesting matches. Bold-street Wesleyans and Orford St. John's were very evehly matched, Orford gaining the victory by 9 runs. L Weaver captured s'x wickets for 26 runs and H Jagger took 3 wickets for 11 runs. The scorine, was low, the best individual effort being F Littleflies 12. _ _ .</p>
        <p>Workingmen's Mission gave Walton Juniors a severe drubbing, the respective totals reaching 129 and 52. For the victors J Seed was at the top of his form and knocked up 44 in grand style.</p>
        <p>Brick-street were victorious over Stockton Heath by a majority of 11. Not one player placed double numbers to his credit.</p>
        <p>Lymm bad a friendly encounter with Flixton, the outcome being a draw greatly in Lymm's favour. L3-mm closed their innings at 126 for 6 wickets and 9of the Flixton wickets fell for 64. For Lymm E. Rouse headed the scores with an excellent 45, while R Bell and A C Saville made 32 and 31 respectively. -- Oughtrington Park cut up badly against Western, who had things all their own way and piled on a margin of 116.0 E Hulton batted brilliantly for his 51. -- Winwick Asylum gained a splendid victory over Monks Hall on Saturday, thanks chiefly to the fine bowling of Dawson (6 wickets for 10 runs) and Hilton (4 wickets for 8 runs), and to the batting of R W Walker who equalled the visitors' total (51) without being cut. Dawson (Winwick) knocked up 37.</p>
        <p>ALL</p>
      </div>
