      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1912-05-11_WidnesExaminer_art0032" n="art0032">
        <head>FACE AND ARM MASS OF BLISTERS</head>
        <p>FACE AND ARM MASS OF BLISTERS</p>
        <p>11, Southgate-road, Winchester, England.—" My injuries to the face and right arm were terrible, caused by an explosion. My face and arm were a mass of blisters. After being treated I found I was unable to go cut without suffaring great pain in the scalded parts. When the wind touched my face the skin cracked. My face was covered in matter-headed pimples, the result of my dreadful scald and my skin was very much inflamed. I used ointments which proved useless and only cauc3d me more pin, and I had to stay indoors for weeks until a trained nurse who visited me recommended Cuticura Soap and Ointment. . -</p>
        <p>1 sent for a sample and after using it was able to go out without any inconvenience. I got some more and used one cake of Cuticura Soap and one box of Cuticura Ointment. Within a month the inflammation went down and I am glad to say my skin has now become quite natural. Cuticura Soap and Cuticura Ointment completely cured me and Cuticura Soap keeps my face in splendid condition." (Signed) Mrs. L. Bowerman, January 13, 1912. Cuticura Soap and Ointment are sold by chemists everywhere. A sample of each with 32-p. book post free from nearest depot : Newbery, 27, Charterhonse Sq., London; IL Towns and Co., Sydney, N.S.W. ; Lennon, Ltd., Cape Town; Muller, Maclean and Co., Calcutta and Bombay; " Cuticnra," Boston, U.S.A. Tender-faced men should shave with Cuticura Soap Shaving Stick. Sample free.</p>
        <p>A wireless plant has been presented to Liverpool Cniversity by Sir Wm. Hartley, and time and weather essages are received daily from the Eiffel Tower.</p>
      </div>
