        <p>"Tell them to open the door," sho said, "it is awful—anything- is preferable to that noi2e</p>
        <p>On Saturday last Italy made a sensational has an area of 400 square miles, and a the navy of Rhodes fought for Pompey. move in the war against Turkey by population of about 30,000. It has a proud The island has been in possession of the occupying, after a bombardment, the Island history, being immensply rich in thc Turks since 1532. Our picture shows a view of Rhodes, in the lEgean Sea. The island Hellinistie Age, and, under the sway of Rome, of Rhodes from the sea. .</p>
        <p>you say now will 'he used in evidence against you!" "This is absurd !" Hawke said contemptu- ously. "The man was supposed to have died in a fire—how could I kill him! Besides, what reason should I have? I befriended him when he was a beggar and came to me for help!,"You know best why you befriended him !" the detective said drily, "and you must not think that there i anything that we don't know, including your murder of Nat Radbourne in Australia years ago— and your theft from Mr. Tennant of 1110 papers that would betray you to him as the man who had deserted his sister !" "Really you seem very well informed," - was the sneering reply, "but may I suggest that all this is a string of nonsense, Mr. Scale? You have not a particle of evidence to help prove all this against me! You Will find that you have made an absurd mis- take !"</p>
        <p>"Not at all, Mr. Hawke," said the man behind the detective, "I can prove every- thing—poor Steinway left a written paper with me the night of his cleat)', in which he related all his interview with you." "This is very amusing!" Clifford Hawke retorted contemptuously, "may I ask who you are, sir?" The stranger stepped forward into the middle of the room.</p>
        <p>"I am Mark Cardew, the man Naho knew you well out in Tarragoola as 'John Ford,' and who gave the police the information that led to your arrest, Clifford Hawke !" (To be.Coneluded.)</p>
