        <p>RUNCORN AND WIDNES. RUNCORN BOARD OF GUARDIANS. The fortnightly meeting of the Runcorn Board of Guardians was held at Dutton on Tuesday. Mr. Spruce presiding. CHILDREN'S lIOME. The Lccal Government Board wrote with regard to the taking over by the Board of Dutton Lodge as a Children's Home. The Local Government Board were advised that certain improvements were necessary in the work of sewage disposal. Subject to these amend- ments and to the estimated cost of the whole of the works being such as the Board might deem reasonable they approved generally of the proposals of the G ardians. CHAPLAINCY. The Local Government Board wrote agreeing to the appointment of the Rev L J T Darwall to the office of Chaplain of the Workhouse, rpFroving of an annual salary of £3O to him. IRE TREATMENT OF FEF.BLE MINDED PATIENTS. The Clerk to the North Western Poor Law Confer- ence wrote ccmmunicating the following resolution reseed at the last conference :--4` Tt at this conference is of the opinion that it is des'rable tt at all Boards of Guardians in tip, area of the North-Western Diarict should avail thearselves of the opportunity offered by the Tervin and Lunesdale Unions to receive the feeble minded adults and children into their institutions at a cost not exceeding 10s. per week." The letter explained that the Lunesdale Ginardians.were prepared to receive children and Tarvin adults. The Board were askei whether they would avail themselves of these exceptional advantages.</p>
